      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-109121",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that a matrix $A$ has characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -5)^{7},$ the nullity of $(A-5I)^{2}$ equals $1,$ and the nullity of $(A-5I)^{3}$ equals $2.$ If a basis of ${R}^{9}$ consists of linearly independent generalized eigenvectors of $A$, how many of these are generalized eigenvectors of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5?$"
