      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-109844",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that a matrix $B$ has characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=(5-\\lambda )^{3}(3+\\lambda )^{9}(\\lambda -\\pi )^{6},$ the nullity of $(B-\\pi I)^{3}$ equals $3,$ and the nullity of $(B-\\pi I)^{4}$ equals $5.$ If a basis of ${R}^{18}$ consists of linearly independent generalized eigenvectors of $B$, how many of these are generalized eigenvectors of rank $4$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\pi ?$"
